          points: [ { point: 'heat flowed from the warmer air into the colder water', marks: 1 }, { point: 'foam is a poor conductor, so heat passed through it slowly and the water gained heat slowly', marks: 1 }, { point: 'foil is a good conductor (or the bare bottle had nothing to slow the heat), so those warmed quickly', marks: 1 } ],
          doNotAccept: ['foam makes cold', 'foam keeps the cold in', 'foil reflects the cold back'],
          // the teacher's ruling, 2026-09-19: partly answered, because it does not say what the heat came from, nor name the other bottles
